{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441147 #edb/ref 1074 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "659100c2-e69a-5015-bd46-ea6499418f4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441148 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $⟨-12,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+9y=42 \\\\ kx+10y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-38$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=456$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441149 #edb/ref 1074 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}42 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =420+36 \\\\  & =456.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{456}{|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =\\frac{456}{-12} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
